===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[conduct]] an experiment.
#: {{ux|en|We're going to '''experiment''' on rats.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=October|title=Models Assist Rolling Stock Design|journal=Railway Magazine|page=647|text=As well as demonstrating operating facilities, full-size car body models are used for '''experimenting''' with new types of interior finish, systems of lighting, positioning of route diagrams and advertisements, and the best form of windscreens at doorways, and the height and location of handgrips and handrails.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[experience]]; to [[feel]]; to [[perceive]]; to [[detect]].
#* '''1662''' Thomas Salusbury, ''Galileo's Dialogue Concerning the Two Chief World Systems'' (Dialogue 2):
#*: ''The Earth, the which may have carried us about perpetually ... without our being ever able to '''experiment''' its rest.''
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[test]] or [[ascertain]] by experiment; to [[try out]]; to make an experiment on.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1481|publisher=William Caxton|title=The Mirrour of the World|section=1.5.22
|passage=''Til they had '''experimented''' whiche was trewe, and who knewe most.''}}

